# Single-point (run 0, no minimization) potential energy evaluation of a
# LigParGen-generated .lmp data file, decomposed by force type. See
# ../README.md's "The LAMMPS leg" section.
#
# Free (non-periodic) boundaries + a cutoff far past the molecule's own
# extent approximates BOSS/OpenMM/NAMD's vacuum, no-cutoff evaluation --
# same reasoning as eval_gromacs_energy.sh's enlarged-box workaround, but
# LAMMPS (unlike modern GROMACS) actually supports true non-periodic
# boundaries directly, so no box enlargement trick is needed here.
units real
atom_style full
boundary f f f

pair_style lj/cut/coul/cut 100.0
bond_style harmonic
angle_style harmonic
dihedral_style opls
improper_style cvff
# OPLS-AA convention: exclude 1-2/1-3 entirely, scale 1-4 by 0.5 for both
# LJ and Coulomb -- matches the coulomb14scale/lj14scale already used by
# LigParGen's OpenMM/GROMACS writers (see docs/adr/0006).
special_bonds lj/coul 0.0 0.0 0.5

read_data __RESID__.lmp

# LAMMPS's default (geometric-mean) pair mixing already matches OPLS-AA's
# own combining rule -- no explicit pair_modify mix needed, since every
# atom in a LigParGen .lmp file gets its own unique type (see
# BOSS2LAMMPS.py), so only diagonal (self) Pair Coeffs are ever given and
# every cross term relies on this mixing rule.

thermo_style custom step ebond eangle edihed eimp evdwl ecoul elong etail epair pe
thermo_modify flush yes
run 0
